<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maroserana dynasty</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Maroserana were a royal dynasty of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a> that rose in the sixteenth and seventeenth centuries. Its branches founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sakalava">Sakalava</a> kingdoms of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menabe">Menabe</a> and Boina on the west coast, and related lines ruled the Mahafaly kingdoms of the south-west. Their power rested on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a>, firearms obtained from European traders, and a royal cult of the ancestors.</p></div>
